# Code Quality

- Match Prettier (single quotes, trailing commas, printWidth 100, Tailwind class sorting).
- Keep TypeScript strict; avoid `any` — prefer `unknown` + narrowing.
- Unused args/vars must be prefixed with `_`.
- Prefer named exports from features; route files may default-export re-exports.
- Run through Husky: `pre-commit` (lint-staged) and `commit-msg` (Conventional Commits).
- Commit types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
- Do not disable lint rules casually; fix the underlying issue.
